{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.SchenstedUninsertInvariants","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SchenstedUninsertInvariants","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.SchenstedReverseCascade"],"declarations":9,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.cornerWitness_noEmptyRows_survives","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.cornerWitness_noEmptyRows_survives","kind":"theorem","line":222,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedUninsertInvariants.lean#L222-L223","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.cornerWitness_rowsSorted_survives","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.cornerWitness_rowsSorted_survives","kind":"theorem","line":217,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedUninsertInvariants.lean#L217-L220","doc":"The same witness, showing the split is real: the two invariants proved above *do* survive the\nstep that breaks `ColStrict`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.cornerWitness_not_colStrict","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.cornerWitness_not_colStrict","kind":"theorem","line":207,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedUninsertInvariants.lean#L207-L215","doc":"**The corner condition is not optional for `ColStrict`** — machine-checked, not asserted.\n\nUndoing at the non-corner row 0 shortens row 0 to `[1]` and leaves row 1 alone, so the shape\nbecomes `(1, 2)` — not a Young diagram — and `StrictBelow` fails on its length half. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.cornerWitness_colStrict","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.cornerWitness_colStrict","kind":"theorem","line":196,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedUninsertInvariants.lean#L196-L205","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.cornerWitness_noEmptyRows","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.cornerWitness_noEmptyRows","kind":"theorem","line":191,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedUninsertInvariants.lean#L191-L194","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.cornerWitness_rowsSorted","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.cornerWitness_rowsSorted","kind":"theorem","line":184,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedUninsertInvariants.lean#L184-L189","doc":"The witness for the corner discussion above: a row-sorted, column-strict tableau with no empty\nrows whose row 0 is *not* a corner — row 1 is exactly as long. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.uninsert_noEmptyRows","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.uninsert_noEmptyRows","kind":"theorem","line":124,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedUninsertInvariants.lean#L124-L182","doc":"**The reverse cascade never leaves an empty row.** A row shortened by `rowUninsert` keeps its\nlength (`rowUninsert_length`); the one row that loses a cell is deleted outright when that would\nempty it, which is the whole reason `uninsert` tests `r.length ≤ 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.uninsert_rowsSorted","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.uninsert_rowsSorted","kind":"theorem","line":70,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedUninsertInvariants.lean#L70-L122","doc":"**The reverse cascade keeps rows weakly increasing.** Each row it touches changes either by\n`dropLast` (a sublist) or by `rowUninsert`, which brick 1's `rowUninsert_sorted` covers; the rest\nare carried through unchanged. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.sorted_dropLast","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.sorted_dropLast","kind":"theorem","line":66,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedUninsertInvariants.lean#L66-L68","doc":"Dropping the last cell keeps a row weakly increasing. ","signatureChunk":0}]}